<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rise, O Voices of Rhodesia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1974">1974</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Rise, O Voices of Rhodesia&quot; was the national anthem of Rhodesia from 1974 to 1979. Rhodesia, a self-governing British colony, was ruled by a predominantly white minority government under Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ian-smith">Ian Smith</a>, which on 11 November 1965 unilaterally declared independence from the United Kingdom rather than accept the British condition of majority rule.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The same melody served as the national anthem of Ian Smith's Rhodesia from 1974 to 1979, as &quot;<b>Rise, O Voices of Rhodesia</b>&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/ode-to-joy">Ode to Joy</a></li><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>Rise, O Voices of Rhodesia</b>&quot; was the national anthem of Rhodesia from 1974 to 1979.</blockquote><a href="/songs/rise-o-voices-of-rhodesia">Rise, O Voices of Rhodesia</a></li></ul></section>
